MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
X-Original-Commit: 81243488c7b81fc388dfa2aaae29e9a412c7151e
X-Original-Committer: Yibo Wang <wyibo6109@gmail.com>
X-Original-Committer-Date: 2026-10-13T01:18:55-05:00

The camera I2C bus (QUP wrap2 SE1, gpio4/5) is physically shared
between the AP and the SEE (sensors execution environment on the
ADSP).  This driver exposes the bus as its own I2C adapter; camera
sensor/VCM children hang under it in DT.

- Default (SEE-owned): nothing in DT occupies gpio4/5, i2c9 stays
  disabled, no geni device exists.  Transfers return -EBUSY.
- Acquired (AP): an SNS/QMI handshake with SEE (attach INIT 0x240 +
  AON camera power-on), then pins mux to qup2_se1 and a geni_i2c
  platform device is instantiated from the disabled i2c9 node.
  Transfers are forwarded.  Release tears the geni down and hands
  the bus back.

All wire formats are fixed-layout packed structs, strictly validated
(libqrtr/libqmi semantics).  Service discovery via in-kernel QRTR
name service.  ACK-driven sequencing, no kernel delays.  Module.

Consumer drivers (smartsens-sc, dw9719) wired via the public API:
probe defers until camres session-ready, acquire in power-on,
release in power-off.  Sensor chip-ID check removed (soldered).

Verified: boot auto-probe at ~25s, 4160x3120@30fps recording,
clean release (clock counts return to zero), SEE recovery.

Co-developed-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Yibo Wang <yibo.wang@opluscamera.com>
